{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":8,"lang":"es","title":"Sé, puedes, haz","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Qué vas a aprender a decir","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"En esta lección aprendes a decir qué sabes hacer y qué no: «sé coser», «no sé patinar». También a pedir: «¿me prestas una pluma?», a dar instrucciones cortas: «conéctalo» — y a decir «no hagas»: «no te apures»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can sew.","translation":"Sé coser.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can't skate.","translation":"No sé patinar.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"Can you lend me a pen?","translation":"¿Me prestas una pluma?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Plug it in.","translation":"Conéctalo.","hi":"Plug"},{"en":"Don't rush.","translation":"No te apures.","hi":"Don't"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"can — «sé», «puedo»","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"can sirve para «sé hacer» y «puedo». Va entre quién y la acción: I can sew. Después de can la acción va como en el diccionario: sin to y sin s. Y no olvides I: «sé coser» es I can sew, no Can sew."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"quién","accent":false},{"text":"can","accent":true},{"text":"acción como en el diccionario","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can sew.","translation":"Sé coser.","hi":"can"},{"en":"He can dance.","translation":"Él sabe bailar.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can speak English.","translation":"Hablo inglés.","hi":"can"},{"en":"He can edit photos.","translation":"Él sabe editar fotos.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can polish shoes.","translation":"Ella sabe lustrar zapatos.","hi":"can"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Can sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"I can to sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"I can sews.","right":"I can sew."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"I can","after":"English.","options":["speak","to speak","speaks"],"answer":"speak","why":"Después de can, la acción va sin to y sin s."}}]},{"num":"03","title":"can no cambia","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"En la lección 6, con he y she la acción llevaba s. Con can no: ni can ni la acción cambian. He can dance, no He cans dance ni He can dances."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"He can dance.","translation":"Él sabe bailar.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can polish shoes.","translation":"Ella sabe lustrar zapatos.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can check the rating.","translation":"Ella puede revisar la calificación.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can give feedback.","translation":"Ella puede dar su opinión.","hi":"can"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"He cans dance.","right":"He can dance."},{"wrong":"He can dances.","right":"He can dance."},{"wrong":"She can to climb.","right":"She can climb."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"spot_slip","kind":"spot_slip","chips":["He","can","dances"],"answerIndex":2,"hint":"Una palabra tiene una letra de más. Tócala.","fix":"Después de can la acción va sin s: He can dance."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"can't — «no sé», «no puedo»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"En español «no» va delante: «no puedo». En inglés la negación va pegada a can: can't. I can't skate — «no sé patinar». Ni I no can ni I don't can."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can't skate.","translation":"No sé patinar.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"She can't ski.","translation":"Ella no sabe esquiar.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"He can't dive.","translation":"Él no sabe bucear.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"I can't make the bed.","translation":"No puedo tender la cama.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"She can't do the ironing.","translation":"Ella no puede planchar la ropa.","hi":"can't"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I no can skate.","right":"I can't skate."},{"wrong":"I don't can skate.","right":"I can't skate."},{"wrong":"She can't skis.","right":"She can't ski."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"No sabes patinar. ¿Cuál es correcta?","optionA":"I no can skate.","optionB":"I can't skate.","correct":"B","explain":"Con can, el «no» es can't."}}]},{"num":"05","title":"Preguntar «¿sabes…?» — Can you…?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Para preguntar si alguien sabe hacer algo, can va al principio: Can you sew? No hace falta Do: can ya hace la pregunta. Respuesta corta: Yes, I can — «sí, sé»."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Can","accent":true},{"text":"quién","accent":false},{"text":"acción","accent":false},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Can you sew?","translation":"¿Sabes coser?","hi":"Can"},{"en":"Can you hike?","translation":"¿Haces senderismo?","hi":"Can"},{"en":"Yes, I can.","translation":"Sí, sé.","hi":"can"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"You can swim?","right":"Can you swim?"},{"wrong":"Do you can swim?","right":"Can you swim?"},{"wrong":"Yes, I can swim it.","right":"Yes, I can."}]}]},{"num":"06","title":"Pedir algo: Can you…?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"La misma pregunta — Can you…? — sirve para pedir: Can you lend me a pen? — «¿me prestas una pluma?». En español también pedimos con «¿puedes…?», así que aquí es igual."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Can you lend me a pen?","translation":"¿Me prestas una pluma?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you unfasten the strap?","translation":"¿Puedes desabrochar la correa?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you check the buckle?","translation":"¿Puedes revisar la hebilla?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you explain it?","translation":"¿Puedes explicarlo?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Can you explain the diagram?","translation":"¿Puedes explicar el diagrama?","hi":"Can you"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Can you to explain it?","right":"Can you explain it?"},{"wrong":"You can lend me a pen?","right":"Can you lend me a pen?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Pide: «¿Puedes explicar el diagrama?»","answer":["Can","you","explain","the","diagram"],"distractors":["to","Do"]}}]},{"num":"07","title":"Instrucción corta: la acción al principio","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Para decir «haz» o «hagan», se empieza directamente con la acción, sin quién: Plug it in — «conéctalo», Buy semi-skimmed milk — «compra leche semidescremada». Es un pedido normal, no suena brusco."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"acción","accent":false},{"text":"qué","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Plug it in.","translation":"Conéctalo.","hi":"Plug"},{"en":"Plug in the humidifier.","translation":"Conecta el humidificador.","hi":"Plug"},{"en":"Turn on the shredder.","translation":"Prende la trituradora.","hi":"Turn on"},{"en":"Buy low-fat yoghurt.","translation":"Compra yogur bajo en grasa.","hi":"Buy"},{"en":"Buy semi-skimmed milk.","translation":"Compra leche semidescremada.","hi":"Buy"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"To plug it in.","right":"Plug it in."}]}]},{"num":"08","title":"«No hagas»: Don't…","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Para decir «no hagas», se pone Don't delante de la acción: Don't rush — «no te apures». No sirve No rush ni Not rush. Para sonar más amable, Please al principio: Please don't interrupt."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"(Please)","accent":false},{"text":"Don't","accent":true},{"text":"acción","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Don't rush.","translation":"No te apures.","hi":"Don't"},{"en":"Don't lean on it.","translation":"No te recargues ahí.","hi":"Don't"},{"en":"Please don't interrupt.","translation":"Por favor, no interrumpas.","hi":"Please don't"},{"en":"Don't spill it.","translation":"No lo derrames.","hi":"Don't"},{"en":"Don't panic.","translation":"No te asustes.","hi":"Don't"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"No rush.","right":"Don't rush."},{"wrong":"No panic.","right":"Don't panic."},{"wrong":"Don't please interrupt.","right":"Please don't interrupt."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"panic.","options":["No","Not","Don't"],"answer":"Don't","why":"«No hagas» es Don't delante de la acción."}}]},{"num":"09","title":"can para ofrecer ayuda y posibilidades","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"can no es solo «sé». También sirve para ofrecer ayuda y hablar de lo que se puede hacer: I can manage the list — «yo puedo llevar la lista», We can share the workload — «podemos repartir el trabajo»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can evaluate it.","translation":"Yo puedo evaluarlo.","hi":"can"},{"en":"We can choose a criterion.","translation":"Podemos elegir un criterio.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can manage the list.","translation":"Yo puedo llevar la lista.","hi":"can"},{"en":"We can share the workload.","translation":"Podemos repartir el trabajo.","hi":"can"},{"en":"I can improve it.","translation":"Yo puedo mejorarlo.","hi":"can"}]}]},{"num":"10","title":"Los errores que comete casi todo el mundo","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Can sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"I can to sew.","right":"I can sew."},{"wrong":"He can dances.","right":"He can dance."},{"wrong":"I no can skate.","right":"I can't skate."},{"wrong":"You can swim?","right":"Can you swim?"},{"wrong":"No rush.","right":"Don't rush."},{"wrong":"Don't please interrupt.","right":"Please don't interrupt."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"can es como un candado para la acción: después de can, la acción siempre va como en el diccionario. Ni to, ni s, ni do."}]},{"num":"11","title":"Qué llevarte a la práctica","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"«Sé, puedo»: I can + acción como en el diccionario. «No sé»: can't. «¿Sabes? ¿Puedes?»: Can you…? «Haz»: la acción al principio. «No hagas»: Don't…, con amabilidad: Please don't…"},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I can speak English.","translation":"Hablo inglés.","hi":"can"},{"en":"She can't ski.","translation":"Ella no sabe esquiar.","hi":"can't"},{"en":"Can you check the buckle?","translation":"¿Puedes revisar la hebilla?","hi":"Can you"},{"en":"Turn on the shredder.","translation":"Prende la trituradora.","hi":"Turn on"},{"en":"Please don't interrupt.","translation":"Por favor, no interrumpas.","hi":"Please don't"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{}}
